FlushRegion: wait for a read's buffer download without holding the buffer cache's lock (UB-153 core).
Contract extracted from zortos293/Lichii 0b83798 (#1028); the GPU thread still waits, see below.
DownloadBufferMemory waited in runtime.Finish() under buffer_cache.mutex, so every guest core that
touched a cached page (OnCPUWrite, GetFlushArea, invalidations) spun for the host GPU round trip of
each reactive flush. FlushRegion now asks DownloadMemoryForRead (lock held) to record the copies of
every buffer in the range into one staging buffer and return the tick; ClearDownload drops pending
fence copies of those bytes as before, but the ranges stay GPU-modified. A throw while recording
cancels it. WaitReadDownload waits for the tick through BufferCacheRuntime::Wait without the lock
(no new scheduler Wait/Finish site in vk_buffer_cache.cpp; runtimes without Wait, OpenGL, never get
a tick and keep DownloadMemory). FinishReadDownload (lock held) writes the copied bytes that are
still GPU-modified (WriteMemory takes invalidated bytes out) and clears the GPU-modified state as
the precise PS5 path did. RasterizerVulkan::OnCPUWrite makes a CPU write into the copies wait until
they land (before the block prepare-vulkan-port.py adapts): core/memory.cpp stores after it returns,
and an exclusive store may fail, so the write goes after the landing as it did when the download
held the lock. Other writes go on; while none is pending the check is one atomic load. A download
recorded between that check and BufferCache::OnCPUWrite is the race main has between OnCPUWrite and
the store. An exception
in the wait cancels the read download: nothing written, ranges still GPU-modified. Only one read
download at a time; another, parameter readbacks (window cache) and non-PS5 builds keep
DownloadMemory.
Not ported: the reading guest thread still waits for the GPU thread (RequestSyncOperation), which
waits for the host GPU itself; upstream lets the GPU thread go on, and that needs every GPU-side
writer of guest memory (memory manager writes, query results, DMA, fence downloads) to land pending
read downloads first. The GPU thread runs nothing else during the wait, so none of them can.
